Are you looking for a varied role in the manufacturing industry? Then we’re looking for you to work for a client in Ittervoort. This is a position as an operator on the mixing line, working in a 3-shift rotation. This means you’ll be responsible for assembling orders. You’ll ensure that the logistics process runs smoothly and that everything is put together properly. Your daily responsibilities will include the following:

- You’ll create the correct combinations and place the products together in the packaging;
- You’ll check that the packages are complete and undamaged as they’re loaded onto the pallets;
- Occasionally moving products with a forklift.

This is a three-shift position, Monday through Friday. You will work the following shifts: 5:54 a.m.–2:00 p.m., 1:54 p.m.–10:00 p.m., 9:54 p.m.–6:00 a.m. (7.36 paid hours).

- You are fluent in Dutch or English;
- You have experience with production work;
- You have experience operating a forklift.
- Would you like to further your career in production? Then we’re looking for you!

Are you a natural leader with experience in logistics? Do you enjoy managing people while continuously improving operational processes? Then this could be the perfect opportunity for you!

We are looking for a Warehouse Supervisor to join an international logistics organization. In this role, you will be responsible for the daily warehouse operation, ensuring your team works safely, efficiently, and delivers the highest quality standards.

What will you do?
As a Warehouse Supervisor, you will lead a team of approximately 15 to 30 warehouse employees and temporary staff. You will be actively present on the warehouse floor and ensure that daily operations run smoothly.

Your responsibilities include:

- Coordinating inbound, storage, and outbound logistics activities;
- Leading, coaching, and motivating warehouse employees;
- Monitoring productivity, planning, and operational quality;
- Ensuring accurate administrative processing within the Warehouse Management System (WMS);
- Identifying operational bottlenecks and driving process improvements;
- Ensuring compliance with safety, quality, and company procedures;
- Conducting performance reviews, coaching sessions, and absence management;
- Working closely with Customer Service and the Warehouse Manager to continuously improve customer satisfaction.

You are a hands-on and motivated supervisor who knows how to inspire a team while maintaining focus on operational excellence.

You also have:

- An MBO Level 4 qualification, preferably in Logistics or Supply Chain;
- At least 2 years of leadership experience within a logistics or production environment;
- Good command of Dutch and/or English;
- Strong communication and leadership skills;
- Experience with warehouse operations and WMS systems;
- You can provide a valid Certificate of Conduct (VOG). If your VOG is approved, Olympia will reimburse the cost of €41.35. If your VOG is not approved, the cost will be at your own expense.
- You have your own accommodation;

Are you looking for a fulltime job in logistics? Would you like to work in a modern, international warehouse where fashion and clothing products are shipped to customers all over the world? Then this opportunity could be perfect for you!

For a large logistics clothing warehouse in Lelystad, we are looking for motivated Production Workers, Warehouse Operatives, and Logistics Associates. You will become part of a friendly international team where teamwork, quality, and a positive working atmosphere are key. On top of that, you can enjoy a delicious hot lunch every working day.

As a Production Worker in the warehouse, you will help ensure that all goods are processed efficiently and accurately. Your tasks will include:

- Loading and unloading trucks;
- Picking and packing customer orders;
- Checking products for quality;
- Unpacking boxes and processing incoming goods;
- Sorting clothing and accessories;
- Maintaining a clean and safe working environment.

This is a full-time position in a 2-shift rotation:

- Morning shift: 07:00 AM - 03:30 PM
- Afternoon shift: 03:00 PM - 11:30 PM

But there is also a nightshift you can work if you want from 23:00 tot 07:30. And there is work in the weekends!

- (Basic) English communication skills, or Polish or Spanish;
- Availability for full-time work in a 2-shift schedule;
- Ability to work effectively in a team;
- Physically fit and comfortable performing active warehouse work;
- Attention to detail and ability to follow instructions;
- Previous logistics or warehouse experience is a plus, but not required.

Summary

Are you detail-oriented, technically minded and do you enjoy working with your hands? Would you like to join one of Europe’s leading manufacturers of custom-made sandwich panels? Then this position with our client in Waalwijk could be the perfect opportunity for you.

Job Description

As a Production Worker, you will contribute to the manufacturing of high-quality, tailor-made sandwich panels. These panels are used in various industries, including bodywork construction and defense. Depending on your experience, interests and the needs of the department, you will be assigned to different tasks within the production process.

You will work from Monday to Friday, from 07:00 to 16:00, as part of a close-knit and supportive team. Using technical drawings and parts lists, you will transform individual raw materials into a finished product of excellent quality. Thanks to the variety of panels and tasks, no two working days are the same.

Accuracy, quality and teamwork are key within this role. The impact of your work is directly visible in the final product.

Responsibilities

Depending on the department, your tasks may include:

- Emptying, cleaning and preparing press tables;
- Collecting and preparing various raw materials;
- Producing and bonding sandwich panels;
- Cutting, deburring and sealing aluminum panels;
- Sawing, calibrating and adjusting materials such as foam, wood and composite to the correct thickness;
- Numbering, sorting and preparing parts for shipment;
- Operating machinery and, if qualified, an overhead crane;
- Maintaining a clean and safe working environment.

What We Ask

- You work accurately and have technical insight;
- You can read technical drawings and parts lists, or are willing to learn;
- You are a true team player;
- You have a good command of Dutch and/or English.

Are you someone who enjoys getting things done and likes working in a modern, well-organized environment? For our client in Montfoort, we are looking for a Warehouse Operative/Orderpicker who will help keep the warehouse running smoothly. You will play an important role in receiving, storing, and shipping goods. This is a full-time position in a fixed shift within a team-oriented environment where collaboration is key and where you will have plenty of opportunities to grow and develop your skills.

As a Warehouse Operative, you play a vital role in the warehouse operation. You ensure that goods are stored in the correct locations, orders are processed on time, and shipments are prepared accurately. You work with attention to detail, think ahead, and maintain an overview in a fast-paced environment. Together with your colleagues, you help ensure that customers can rely on fast and dependable deliveries.

Your responsibilities include:

- Picking orders using handheld scanners and the Warehouse Management System (WMS);
- Checking incoming goods for quantity and quality;
- Moving and storing goods in the correct warehouse locations;
- Preparing orders for shipment, including labeling, packing, and final inspections;
- Loading and unloading trucks;
- Recording the movement of goods in the system;
- Identifying discrepancies and contributing ideas for process improvements;
- Supporting colleagues with various warehouse tasks.

You will work 40 hours per week and can choose between two shifts:

- Morning shift: 07:00 AM – 04:00 PM
- Evening shift: 04:00 PM – 01:00 AM

You will remain in the same shift at all times, allowing you to maintain a consistent work schedule and routine.

For this position, we are looking for someone who:

- Has an MBO level of education and thinking ability (vocational education level);
- Is proactive, accurate, and detail-oriented;
- Speaks Dutch or English;
- Has their own transportation and can reliably arrive at the workplace on time.
